	"metadata": {
		"app_version": "0.1.0",
		"created": "2026-10-18T12:00:00",
		"description": "Firmware example: a DHT22 temperature/humidity sensor on D2 (through the virtual pin P1) and a 16x2 I2C LCD, both firmware-driven. The sketch firmware/sketches/env_logger reads the sensor and prints the reading to the LCD and serial.",
		"measurement": "Compile firmware/sketches/env_logger for arduino:avr:uno, then run_firmware(hex_path, attach_devices=true, pin_map={\"2\": \"P1\"}). The DHT1 temp_c/humidity parameters are what the sensor reports and the LCD1 shows; firmware/sketches/env_logger writes \"T=23.0C H=48.0%\" to the LCD and serial. Only the sensor and the display are modelled: the two wires between the MCU and the modules are drawn as virtual pins.",
		"modified": "2026-10-18T12:00:00",
		"name": "Firmware Environment Logger (DHT22 + I2C LCD)"
	},
